MODULE landscape

PUBLIC CONSTANT LANDSCAPE STORAGE KEY
    browser storage identifier for format version 1

PUBLIC CONSTANT LANDSCAPE VERSION
    current supported format version

PUBLIC CONSTANT MAXIMUM USER ROCK COUNT
    eight rocks

PUBLIC FUNCTION SCREEN RAY
INPUT
    clicked screen position
    canvas bounds
    camera position
    camera look-at point
OUTPUT
    normalized world direction
BEHAVIOR
    reject empty canvas bounds and degenerate camera vectors
    convert the click to aspect-correct shader screen coordinates
    build the same camera basis used for rendering
    return the normalized world direction through the click

PUBLIC FUNCTION TERRAIN DISTANCE AT
INPUT
    world point
    terrain scale, height, octave count, and seed
OUTPUT
    signed distance from the generated terrain
BEHAVIOR
    calculate repeatable value noise from the seed
    use the requested 1 through 12 octave count for ridged terrain detail
    use up to four requested octaves for domain warping and broad shape noise
    combine broad and ridged noise on the same stationary surface used by rendering
    return world height minus generated terrain height

PUBLIC FUNCTION TERRAIN HIT
INPUT
    ray origin
    normalized ray direction
    terrain settings
OUTPUT
    terrain WorldPosition or no result
BEHAVIOR
    advance along the ray by the terrain distance
    return the sampled point when it reaches the surface tolerance
    return no result after the sample limit, distance limit, invalid travel, or travel behind the origin

PUBLIC FUNCTION VALIDATE LANDSCAPE
INPUT
    candidate value
OUTPUT
    validated Landscape
BEHAVIOR
    require exactly the documented top-level and nested fields
    require supported version, finite values, documented ranges, exact colour strings, and at most eight rocks
    reject the entire candidate on the first invalid field with expected and received details
    return a complete validated copy without converting invalid values
